 ## Background
-Originated from the DreamGaussian project, which integrates diffusion models into 3D Gaussian Splatting optimization pipelines [S1, unofficial]. The method leverages the DDIM sampler and classifier-free guidance to provide gradient signals from a frozen Stable Diffusion model for optimizing radiance fields or latent representations [S1, unofficial].
+The method is implemented in the DreamGaussian codebase as part of a diffusion-based optimization loop for radiance fields [S1, unofficial]. It provides gradient signals from a frozen Stable Diffusion model by predicting noise, applying classifier-free guidance, and backpropagating the difference between predicted and actual noise [S1, unofficial].
 
